  "body": "@mfreed7 seems to have introduced [a WPT](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/syntax/serializing-html-fragments/escaping.html) which expects different serialization behavior in `<noscript>` elements depending on whether the document is scripting-enabled or not. I can't find any backing for this in the spec, and the [commit message](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/65e68547032c551e8765245621a9aac70e5d5a3d) notes significant interop differences. [The WPT results dashboard is also grim](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/syntax/serializing-html-fragments/escaping.html?label=master&label=experimental&product=chrome&product=firefox&product=safari&aligned&q=escaping.html).\r\n\r\nIt would be good to re-align the tests with the spec, or the spec with the tests, probably following some cross-browser discussion.\r\n\r\n/cc @whatwg/html-parser ",
